#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Writing a GEOM Class"
msgstr "编写 GEOM 类"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:43
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr "摘要"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:46
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This text documents some starting points in developing GEOM classes, and "
"kernel modules in general.  It is assumed that the reader is familiar with C "
"userland programming."
msgstr "本文介绍开发 GEOM 类以及一般内核模块的一些入门知识。假定读者熟悉 C 用户空间编程。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:48
msgid "'''"
msgstr "'''"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "介绍"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:55
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "文档"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:59
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Documentation on kernel programming is scarce - it is one of few areas where "
"there is nearly nothing in the way of friendly tutorials, and the phrase "
"\"use the source!\" really holds true.  However, there are some bits and "
"pieces (some of them seriously outdated) floating around that should be "
"studied before beginning to code:"
msgstr "关于内核编程的文档十分稀少——这是少数几乎没有友好教程的领域之一，而“使用源代码！”这句话确实名副其实。不过，仍有一些零散资料（其中一些已经严重过时）值得在开始编码前阅读："

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:61
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The extref:{developers-handbook}[FreeBSD Developer's Handbook] - part of the "
"documentation project, it does not contain anything specific to kernel "
"programming, but rather some general useful information."
msgstr "extref:{developers-handbook}[FreeBSD 开发者手册]——它是文档项目的一部分，不包含内核编程的专门内容，但提供了一些有用的通用信息。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:62
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The extref:{arch-handbook}[FreeBSD Architecture Handbook] - also from the "
"documentation project, contains descriptions of several low-level facilities "
"and procedures. The most important chapter is 13, extref:{arch-handbook}"
"[Writing FreeBSD device drivers, driverbasics]."
msgstr "extref:{arch-handbook}[FreeBSD 架构手册]——同样来自文档项目，介绍了若干底层设施和过程。最重要的是第 13 章：extref:{arch-handbook}[编写 FreeBSD 设备驱动程序，driverbasics]。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:63
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Blueprints section of http://www.freebsddiary.org[FreeBSD Diary] web "
"site - contains several interesting articles on kernel facilities."
msgstr "link:http://www.freebsddiary.org[FreeBSD Diary] 网站的 Blueprints 部分——其中包含一些关于内核设施的有趣文章。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:64
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man pages in section 9 - for important documentation on kernel functions."
msgstr "第 9 节中的手册页——提供重要的内核函数文档。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:65
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man:geom[4] man page and http://phk.freebsd.dk/pubs/[PHK's GEOM slides] "
"- for general introduction of the GEOM subsystem."
msgstr "man:geom[4] 手册页和 link:http://phk.freebsd.dk/pubs/[PHK 的 GEOM 幻灯片]——提供 GEOM 子系统的一般介绍。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:66
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Man pages man:g_bio[9], man:g_event[9], man:g_data[9], man:g_geom[9], man:"
"g_provider[9], man:g_consumer[9], man:g_access[9] & others linked from "
"those, for documentation on specific functionalities."
msgstr "man:g_bio[9]、man:g_event[9]、man:g_data[9]、man:g_geom[9]、man:g_provider[9]、man:g_consumer[9]、man:g_access[9] 等手册页，以及这些页面链接到的其他页面——提供特定功能的文档。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:67
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The man:style[9] man page - for documentation on the coding-style "
"conventions which must be followed for any code which is to be committed to "
"the FreeBSD tree."
msgstr "man:style[9] 手册页——介绍提交到 FreeBSD 源代码树的代码必须遵循的编码风格约定。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:69
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Preliminaries"
msgstr "准备工作"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:76
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The best way to do kernel development is to have (at least) two separate "
"computers.  One of these would contain the development environment and "
"sources, and the other would be used to test the newly written code by "
"network-booting and network-mounting filesystems from the first one.  This "
"way if the new code contains bugs and crashes the machine, it will not mess "
"up the sources (and other \"live\" data).  The second system does not even "
"require a proper display.  Instead, it could be connected with a serial "
"cable or KVM to the first one."
msgstr "进行内核开发的最佳方式是至少准备两台独立的计算机。一台用于开发环境和源代码，另一台通过网络启动并从第一台计算机挂载文件系统，以测试新编写的代码。这样，如果新代码包含错误并导致机器崩溃，也不会破坏源代码（及其他“正在使用”的数据）。第二台系统甚至不需要配备显示器，可以通过串口线或 KVM 连接到第一台系统。"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:79
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"But, since not everybody has two or more computers handy, there are a few "
"things that can be done to prepare an otherwise \"live\" system for "
"developing kernel code.  This setup is also applicable for developing in a "
"http://www.vmware.com/[VMWare] or http://www.qemu.org/[QEmu] virtual machine "
"(the next best thing after a dedicated development machine)."
msgstr "不过，并非每个人都随手有两台或更多计算机，因此可以采取一些措施，为其他“正在使用”的系统做好内核代码开发准备。此配置也适用于在 link:http://www.vmware.com/[VMWare] 或 link:http://www.qemu.org/[QEmu] 虚拟机中开发（仅次于专用开发计算机的最佳选择）。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:81
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Modifying a System for Development"
msgstr "为开发修改系统"

#. type: .abstract-title
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:84
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For any kernel programming a kernel with `INVARIANTS` enabled is a must-"
"have. So enter these in your kernel configuration file:"
msgstr "进行任何内核编程都必须启用 `INVARIANTS` 的内核。因此，请将以下选项加入内核配置文件："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:89
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"options INVARIANT_SUPPORT\n"
"options INVARIANTS\n"
msgstr "options INVARIANT_SUPPORT\noptions INVARIANTS\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:92
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For more debugging you should also include WITNESS support, which will alert "
"you of mistakes in locking:"
msgstr "如需更多调试功能，还应启用 WITNESS 支持，它会提示锁使用方面的错误："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:97
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"options WITNESS_SUPPORT\n"
"options WITNESS\n"
msgstr "options WITNESS_SUPPORT\noptions WITNESS\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:100
#, fuzzy
msgid "For debugging crash dumps, a kernel with debug symbols is needed:"
msgstr "要调试崩溃转储，需要使用带有调试符号的内核："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:104
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  makeoptions    DEBUG=-g\n"
msgstr "  makeoptions    DEBUG=-g\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:109
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With the usual way of installing the kernel (`make installkernel`) the debug "
"kernel will not be automatically installed.  It is called [.filename]#kernel."
"debug# and located in [.filename]#/usr/obj/usr/src/sys/KERNELNAME/#.  For "
"convenience it should be copied to [.filename]#/boot/kernel/#."
msgstr "使用常规方式安装内核（`make installkernel`）时，不会自动安装调试内核。它名为 [.filename]#kernel.debug#，位于 [.filename]#/usr/obj/usr/src/sys/KERNELNAME/#。为方便使用，应将其复制到 [.filename]#/boot/kernel/#。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:112
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Another convenience is enabling the kernel debugger so you can examine a "
"kernel panic when it happens.  For this, enter the following lines in your "
"kernel configuration file:"
msgstr "另一个便利之处是启用内核调试器，以便在发生内核崩溃时检查内核。为此，请在内核配置文件中加入以下几行："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:118
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"options KDB\n"
"options DDB\n"
"options KDB_TRACE\n"
msgstr "options KDB\noptions DDB\noptions KDB_TRACE\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:121
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For this to work you might need to set a sysctl (if it is not on by default):"
msgstr "要使其正常工作，可能需要设置一个 sysctl（如果默认未启用）："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:125
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  debug.debugger_on_panic=1\n"
msgstr "  debug.debugger_on_panic=1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:133
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kernel panics will happen, so care should be taken with the filesystem "
"cache.  In particular, having softupdates might mean the latest file version "
"could be lost if a panic occurs before it is committed to storage.  "
"Disabling softupdates yields a great performance hit, and still does not "
"guarantee data consistency.  Mounting filesystem with the \"sync\" option is "
"needed for that.  For a compromise, the softupdates cache delays can be "
"shortened.  There are three sysctl's that are useful for this (best to be "
"set in [.filename]#/etc/sysctl.conf#):"
msgstr "内核崩溃时有发生，因此应注意文件系统缓存。特别是，启用 softupdates 时，如果崩溃发生在最新文件版本提交到存储设备之前，该版本可能会丢失。禁用 softupdates 会严重影响性能，而且仍无法保证数据一致性。要保证一致性，需要使用 \"sync\" 选项挂载文件系统。折中方案是缩短 softupdates 缓存延迟。以下三个 sysctl 对此很有用（最好将其设置在 [.filename]#/etc/sysctl.conf# 中）："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:139
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"kern.filedelay=5\n"
"kern.dirdelay=4\n"
"kern.metadelay=3\n"
msgstr "kern.filedelay=5\nkern.dirdelay=4\nkern.metadelay=3\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:142
#, fuzzy
msgid "The numbers represent seconds."
msgstr "这些数值的单位是秒。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:150
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For debugging kernel panics, kernel core dumps are required.  Since a kernel "
"panic might make filesystems unusable, this crash dump is first written to a "
"raw partition.  Usually, this is the swap partition.  This partition must be "
"at least as large as the physical RAM in the machine.  On the next boot, the "
"dump is copied to a regular file.  This happens after filesystems are "
"checked and mounted, and before swap is enabled.  This is controlled with "
"two [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# variables:"
msgstr "调试内核崩溃需要内核核心转储。由于内核崩溃可能导致文件系统无法使用，崩溃转储会先写入原始分区，通常是交换分区。该分区必须至少与机器的物理内存一样大。下次启动时，转储会被复制到普通文件中。此操作会在检查并挂载文件系统之后、启用交换空间之前进行。此行为由 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中的两个变量控制："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:155
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"dumpdev=\"/dev/ad0s4b\"\n"
"dumpdir=\"/usr/core\"\n"
msgstr "dumpdev=\"/dev/ad0s4b\"\ndumpdir=\"/usr/core\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:158
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The `dumpdev` variable specifies the swap partition and `dumpdir` tells the "
"system where in the filesystem to relocate the core dump on reboot."
msgstr "`dumpdev` 变量指定交换分区，`dumpdir` 则告知系统在重新启动时将核心转储移到文件系统中的哪个位置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:161
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Writing kernel core dumps is slow and takes a long time so if you have lots "
"of memory (>256M) and lots of panics it could be frustrating to sit and wait "
"while it is done (twice - first to write it to swap, then to relocate it to "
"filesystem).  It is convenient then to limit the amount of RAM the system "
"will use via a [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# tunable:"
msgstr "写入内核核心转储速度很慢，需要很长时间。因此，如果内存较大（>256M）且内核经常崩溃，等待转储完成可能会让人十分沮丧（转储要写入两次：先写入交换分区，再移到文件系统中）。此时，可以通过 [.filename]#/boot/loader.conf# 中的可调参数限制系统使用的内存量："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:165
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  hw.physmem=\"256M\"\n"
msgstr "  hw.physmem=\"256M\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:168
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If the panics are frequent and filesystems large (or you simply do not trust "
"softupdates+background fsck) it is advisable to turn background fsck off via "
"[.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# variable:"
msgstr "如果崩溃频繁且文件系统很大（或者你就是不信任 softupdates 和后台 fsck），建议通过 [.filename]#/etc/rc.conf# 中的变量关闭后台 fsck："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:172
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  background_fsck=\"NO\"\n"
msgstr "  background_fsck=\"NO\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:177
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This way, the filesystems will always get checked when needed.  Note that "
"with background fsck, a new panic could happen while it is checking the "
"disks.  Again, the safest way is not to have many local filesystems by using "
"another computer as an NFS server."
msgstr "这样，文件系统就会在需要时始终得到检查。请注意，启用后台 fsck 时，检查磁盘期间可能再次发生崩溃。同样，最安全的做法是将另一台计算机用作 NFS 服务器，从而减少本地文件系统的数量。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:179
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Starting the Project"
msgstr "启动项目"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:183
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For the purpose of creating a new GEOM class, an empty subdirectory has to "
"be created under an arbitrary user-accessible directory.  You do not have to "
"create the module directory under [.filename]#/usr/src#."
msgstr "要创建新的 GEOM 类，必须在任意一个用户可访问的目录下创建一个空子目录。模块目录不必建在 [.filename]#/usr/src# 下。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:185
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "The Makefile"
msgstr "Makefile"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:188
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"It is good practice to create [.filename]#Makefiles# for every nontrivial "
"coding project, which of course includes kernel modules."
msgstr "为每个非简单的编码项目创建 [.filename]#Makefiles# 是一种良好实践，内核模块当然也不例外。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:191
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Creating the [.filename]#Makefile# is simple thanks to an extensive set of "
"helper routines provided by the system.  In short, here is how a minimal [."
"filename]#Makefile# looks for a kernel module:"
msgstr "借助系统提供的大量辅助例程，创建 [.filename]#Makefile# 很简单。下面是内核模块的最简 [.filename]#Makefile# 示例："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:196
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ""
"SRCS=g_journal.c\n"
"KMOD=geom_journal\n"
msgstr "SRCS=g_journal.c\nKMOD=geom_journal\n"

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:198
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid ".include <bsd.kmod.mk>\n"
msgstr ".include <bsd.kmod.mk>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:202
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This [.filename]#Makefile# (with changed filenames) will do for any kernel "
"module, and a GEOM class can reside in just one kernel module.  If more than "
"one file is required, list it in the `SRCS` variable, separated with "
"whitespace from other filenames."
msgstr "这个 [.filename]#Makefile#（替换文件名后）适用于任何内核模块，而一个 GEOM 类可以只包含在一个内核模块中。如果需要多个文件，请将它们列入 `SRCS` 变量，并用空格与其他文件名分隔。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:204
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "On FreeBSD Kernel Programming"
msgstr "FreeBSD 内核编程"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:207
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Memory Allocation"
msgstr "内存分配"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:212
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"See man:malloc[9].  Basic memory allocation is only slightly different than "
"its userland equivalent.  Most notably, `malloc`() and `free`() accept "
"additional parameters as is described in the man page."
msgstr "请参见 man:malloc[9]。基本内存分配与用户空间中的对应方式只有少许不同。最明显的是，`malloc`() 和 `free`() 接受额外参数，具体说明见手册页。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:214
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"A \"malloc type\" must be declared in the declaration section of a source "
"file, like this:"
msgstr "必须在源文件的声明部分声明一种“malloc 类型”，例如："

#. type: delimited block . 4
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:218
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "  static MALLOC_DEFINE(M_GJOURNAL, \"gjournal data\", \"GEOM_JOURNAL Data\");\n"
msgstr "  static MALLOC_DEFINE(M_GJOURNAL, \"gjournal data\", \"GEOM_JOURNAL Data\");\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:221
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To use this macro, [.filename]#sys/param.h#, [.filename]#sys/kernel.h# and [."
"filename]#sys/malloc.h# headers must be included."
msgstr "要使用此宏，必须包含 [.filename]#sys/param.h#、[.filename]#sys/kernel.h# 和 [.filename]#sys/malloc.h# 头文件。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:224
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There is another mechanism for allocating memory, the UMA (Universal Memory "
"Allocator).  See man:uma[9] for details, but it is a special type of "
"allocator mainly used for speedy allocation of lists comprised of same-sized "
"items (for example, dynamic arrays of structs)."
msgstr "还有另一种内存分配机制：UMA（通用内存分配器）。详情请参见 man:uma[9]。这是一种特殊类型的分配器，主要用于快速分配由相同大小元素组成的列表（例如结构体的动态数组）。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:226
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Lists and Queues"
msgstr "列表和队列"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:233
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"See man:queue[3].  There are a LOT of cases when a list of things needs to "
"be maintained.  Fortunately, this data structure is implemented (in several "
"ways) by C macros included in the system.  The most used list type is TAILQ "
"because it is the most flexible.  It is also the one with largest memory "
"requirements (its elements are doubly-linked) and also the slowest (although "
"the speed variation is on the order of several CPU instructions more, so it "
"should not be taken seriously)."
msgstr "请参见 man:queue[3]。很多情况下都需要维护事物列表。幸运的是，系统通过 C 宏实现了这种数据结构（有多种形式）。最常用的列表类型是 TAILQ，因为它最灵活。它的内存需求也最大（元素采用双向链表），速度也最慢（不过速度差异仅相当于多执行几条 CPU 指令，因此不必太在意）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:235
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If data retrieval speed is very important, see man:tree[3] and man:"
"hashinit[9]."
msgstr "如果数据检索速度非常重要，请参见 man:tree[3] 和 man:hashinit[9]。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:237
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "BIOs"
msgstr "BIO"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:241
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Structure `bio` is used for any and all Input/Output operations concerning "
"GEOM.  It basically contains information about what device ('provider') "
"should satisfy the request, request type, offset, length, pointer to a "
"buffer, and a bunch of \"user-specific\" flags and fields that can help "
"implement various hacks."
msgstr "`bio` 结构用于 GEOM 涉及的所有输入/输出操作。它基本上包含要满足请求的设备（“provider”）、请求类型、偏移量、长度、缓冲区指针，以及一系列有助于实现各种变通方案的“用户专用”标志和字段。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:245
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The important thing here is that ``bio``s are handled asynchronously.  That "
"means that, in most parts of the code, there is no analogue to userland's "
"man:read[2] and man:write[2] calls that do not return until a request is "
"done.  Rather, a developer-supplied function is called as a notification "
"when the request gets completed (or results in error)."
msgstr "这里重要的一点是，``bio`` 操作以异步方式处理。这意味着，在大多数代码中，没有类似于用户空间 man:read[2] 和 man:write[2] 的调用，能够一直等待到请求完成。相反，请求完成（或出错）时会调用开发者提供的函数作为通知。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:249
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The asynchronous programming model (also called \"event-driven\") is "
"somewhat harder than the much more used imperative one used in userland (at "
"least it takes a while to get used to it).  In some cases the helper "
"routines `g_write_data`() and `g_read_data`() can be used, but __not "
"always__.  In particular, they cannot be used when a mutex is held; for "
"example, the GEOM topology mutex or the internal mutex held during the `."
"start`() and `.stop`() functions."
msgstr "异步编程模型（也称为“事件驱动”）比用户空间中更常用的命令式编程模型要难一些（至少需要一段时间来适应）。某些情况下可以使用辅助例程 `g_write_data`() 和 `g_read_data`()，但__并非总是如此__。尤其是在持有互斥锁时不能使用它们，例如 GEOM 拓扑互斥锁，或在 `.start`() 和 `.stop`() 函数期间持有的内部互斥锁。"

#. type: Title ==
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:251
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "On GEOM Programming"
msgstr "GEOM 编程"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:254
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Ggate"
msgstr "Ggate"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:258
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If maximum performance is not needed, a much simpler way of making a data "
"transformation is to implement it in userland via the ggate (GEOM gate) "
"facility.  Unfortunately, there is no easy way to convert between, or even "
"share code between the two approaches."
msgstr "如果不需要最高性能，更简单的数据转换方式是在用户空间中通过 ggate（GEOM gate）设施实现。遗憾的是，这两种方法之间既难以转换，也难以共享代码。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:260
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "GEOM Class"
msgstr "GEOM 类"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:265
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"GEOM classes are transformations on the data.  These transformations can be "
"combined in a tree-like fashion.  Instances of GEOM classes are called "
"__geoms__."
msgstr "GEOM 类用于转换数据。这些转换可以树状方式组合。GEOM 类的实例称为 __geoms__。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:267
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Each GEOM class has several \"class methods\" that get called when there is "
"no geom instance available (or they are simply not bound to a single "
"instance):"
msgstr "每个 GEOM 类都有若干“类方法”，当没有可用的 geom 实例时（或这些方法并未绑定到单个实例时）会调用它们："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:269
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`.init` is called when GEOM becomes aware of a GEOM class (when the kernel "
"module gets loaded.)"
msgstr "当 GEOM 感知到某个 GEOM 类时（即内核模块加载时），会调用 `.init`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:270
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`.fini` gets called when GEOM abandons the class (when the module gets "
"unloaded)"
msgstr "当 GEOM 放弃某个类时（即模块卸载时），会调用 `.fini`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:271
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`.taste` is called next, once for each provider the system has available. If "
"applicable, this function will usually create and start a geom instance."
msgstr "接下来，对系统中可用的每个 provider 调用一次 `.taste`。如果适用，此函数通常会创建并启动一个 geom 实例。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:272
#, fuzzy
msgid "`.destroy_geom` is called when the geom should be disbanded"
msgstr "需要解散 geom 时会调用 `.destroy_geom`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:273
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"`.ctlconf` is called when user requests reconfiguration of existing geom"
msgstr "用户请求重新配置现有 geom 时会调用 `.ctlconf`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:275
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Also defined are the GEOM event functions, which will get copied to the geom "
"instance."
msgstr "此外还定义了 GEOM 事件函数，这些函数会被复制到 geom 实例中。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:277
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Field `.geom` in the `g_class` structure is a LIST of geoms instantiated "
"from the class."
msgstr "`g_class` 结构中的 `.geom` 字段是从该类实例化的 geom 列表。"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:279
#, fuzzy
msgid "These functions are called from the g_event kernel thread."
msgstr "这些函数由 g_event 内核线程调用。"

#. type: Title ===
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:281
#, no-wrap, fuzzy
msgid "Softc"
msgstr "Softc"

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:287
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The name \"softc\" is a legacy term for \"driver private data\".  The name "
"most probably comes from the archaic term \"software control block\".  In "
"GEOM, it is a structure (more precise: pointer to a structure) that can be "
"attached to a geom instance to hold whatever data is private to the geom "
"instance.  Most GEOM classes have the following members:"
msgstr "“softc”是“驱动程序私有数据”的旧称。这个名称很可能源自过时的术语“软件控制块”。在 GEOM 中，它是一种结构（更准确地说，是指向结构的指针），可附加到 geom 实例，用来存放该实例的任意私有数据。大多数 GEOM 类都包含以下成员："

#. type: Plain text
#: documentation/content/en/articles/geom-class/_index.adoc:289
#, fuzzy
msgid "`struct g_provider *provider` : The \"provider\" this geom instantiates"
